sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Customer
    participant Agent as Agent Orchestrator
    participant Router as Tool Router
    participant Security as Identity and Permission Checks
    participant Confirm as Confirmation Manager
    participant Banking as Banking API
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant Audit as Audit Logging

    Customer->>Agent: Request account-specific operation
    Agent->>Router: Propose approved tool and validated arguments
    Router->>Security: Authorize tool for trusted customer context
    Note over Router,Security: Customer identity is derived from trusted authentication/session context, never from model-supplied customer IDs.

    alt Identity or permission check fails
        Security-->>Router: Deny
        Router->>Audit: Record denied tool call and redacted inputs
        Router-->>Agent: Authorization failure
        Agent-->>Customer: Explain limitation or offer human handoff
    else Authorization succeeds
        Security-->>Router: Permit tool invocation
        Router->>Router: Validate schema, required fields, and action risk

        alt Read-only operation
            Router->>Banking: Invoke approved read operation with trusted identity
            Banking->>DB: Read authorized banking records
            DB-->>Banking: Records or no matching result
            Banking-->>Router: Result or explicit not-found response
            Router->>Audit: Record tool name, redacted inputs, result status
            Router-->>Agent: Structured result
            Agent->>Agent: Interpret result without inventing missing facts
            Agent-->>Customer: Answer or explain that information is unavailable
        else Consequential operation requiring confirmation
            Router->>Confirm: Request or validate pending confirmation
            Confirm->>DB: Load or create action-bound pending confirmation
            DB-->>Confirm: Confirmation state

            alt No valid confirmation exists
                Confirm->>Audit: Record confirmation request
                Confirm-->>Router: Confirmation required; no execution
                Router->>Audit: Record tool call outcome
                Router-->>Agent: Pending confirmation details
                Agent-->>Customer: Summarize exact action and ask for explicit approval
            else Confirmation is valid, unexpired, and unused
                Confirm-->>Router: One-time approval for bound action
                Router->>Banking: Execute approved operation with idempotency key
                Banking->>DB: Recheck authorization and apply transactional state change
                alt Operation succeeds
                    DB-->>Banking: Commit result
                    Banking->>DB: Persist operation audit record
                    Banking-->>Router: Success with operation reference
                else Operation is rejected
                    DB-->>Banking: No successful state change
                    Banking->>DB: Persist rejection/audit outcome
                    Banking-->>Router: Explicit failure
                else Outcome is unknown (for example, timeout)
                    Banking-->>Router: Outcome unresolved
                    Note over Banking,DB: Reconcile by operation reference/idempotency key before retrying or claiming success/failure.
                end
                Router->>Audit: Record final or unresolved tool outcome
                Router-->>Agent: Structured outcome
                Agent->>Agent: Ensure response matches authoritative outcome
                Agent-->>Customer: Report confirmed result or explain unresolved status
            end
        else Tool input is invalid
            Router->>Audit: Record validation failure with redacted inputs
            Router-->>Agent: Validation error; operation not executed
            Agent-->>Customer: Ask for missing or corrected information
        end
    end

    Note over Agent,DB: The model proposes actions; backend services enforce identity, permissions, confirmation, and execution.
    Note over Confirm,DB: Pending confirmations are persistent, action-bound, expiring, single-use, and auditable.
    Note over Audit: Every tool call is logged with tool name, redacted inputs, result/status, and correlation context.
